{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794997651,"nonce":"TcayhYbwGQtrfroLG8hMuhBGu5g=","title":"Meshing leaves the main thread at one OpenMP thread, so un-compiled OpenMP work runs serially","message":"After a mesh has been generated, the main thread's OpenMP thread count is 1 and stays there. Every OpenMP library called from the main thread afterwards runs on one thread: in particular an un-compiled `fem.solve(linear=jno.solve.lu(backend=\"pardiso\"))`, whose symbolic analysis is then planned for one thread and stays serial for the life of the cached factorization, also for later compiled calls.\n\nReproduction (prints the count of the main thread; it drops at the first call that needs the mesh):\n\n```python\nimport ctypes\nimport jno\n\ndef omp_threads():\n    lib = [l.split()[-1] for l in open(\"/proc/self/maps\") if \"libomp\" in l or \"libgomp\" in l or \"libiomp\" in l][0]\n    return ctypes.CDLL(lib).omp_get_max_threads()\n\nimport pypardiso  # loads an OpenMP runtime\nprint(\"start\", omp_threads())\nd = jno.shape.box(0, 0, 0, 4, 1, 1, size=0.25).domain()\nprint(\"after domain()\", omp_threads())\nd.fem_symbols(space=\"P0\", names=(\"r\", \"s\"))\nprint(\"after fem_symbols\", omp_threads())   # 1\n```\n\nLikely cause, not confirmed: the mesh generator applies its `General.NumThreads` option with `omp_set_num_threads`, which changes the calling thread only and is never restored (`jno/geometry/emit.py`, `jno/domain/polygon_domain.py` set that option).\n\nWanted: the thread count of the calling thread is the same before and after a domain is built. A test can assert `omp_get_max_threads()` around `jno.shape...domain()` plus the first call that meshes.\n\nSeen while fixing the PARDISO thread-count defect: that fix makes the mismatch harmless, but the serial factorization from the main thread remains (a numeric factorization analysed on one thread was measured several times slower than one analysed on all cores).","files":null}]}